API/RPC Contract — Hausa
Ka'idar identity
Admin console: Supabase Auth identity (auth.uid()) + AAL2 MFA.
Contributor candidate: API ta tabbatar da Pi access token, ta samo Pi UID daga verified response.
A tabbatar da mapping tsakanin Pi UID da Supabase Auth UID ta hanyar approved server-side binding; kada browser ya tura pi_uid a matsayin hujja.
Mainnet admin authorization data daga ALBUKHR Mainnet Supabase kawai.
Proposed endpoints (ba a aiwatar ba)
POST /api/admin/contributor-admin/nominations
Auth: Supabase session, AAL2, active super_admin.
Body: candidate contributor identifier, proposed narrow permission profile, reason, expiry.
Server validates candidate exists on Mainnet; logs contributor_admin_nomination_created.
Returns nomination ID + one-time opaque invitation token (only once); store only hash.
No role grant occurs.
GET /api/contributor-admin/application?token=...
Auth: verified Pi session + valid invitation token.
Returns minimum data needed for candidate to confirm application and consent.
No admin role is returned or created.
POST /api/contributor-admin/application
Auth: verified Pi session; token is single-use, expiring, revocable.
Captures profile/consent version and private selfie object reference created via server-approved upload flow.
Camera-only UI: no file picker. Server cannot assume camera capture alone proves liveness.
Status becomes submitted_pending_review; no admin access.
POST /api/admin/contributor-admin/applications/:id/review
Auth: AAL2 + active super_admin.
Decision: approve or reject; reason required for rejection.
Approval alone may mark identity review complete, but role grant is a separate explicit action.
All reads of sensitive selfie/profile are audited.
POST /api/admin/contributor-admin/assignments
Auth: AAL2 + active super_admin.
Re-verify candidate, application approved, policy consent current, MFA requirement, no conflicting status.
Grant only contributor_admin; do not accept arbitrary role string.
Use existing admin_users + admin_role_assignments; atomic transaction and audit.
Role scope limited to enumerated Contributor tasks; deny finance, treasury, withdrawals, payout, role management, RLS changes, testnet admin access.
DELETE /api/admin/contributor-admin/assignments/:id
Auth: AAL2 + active super_admin.
Set active=false and revoked_at/revoked_by; preserve historical record.
Audit event in same transaction.
Revocation must take effect immediately on API/database authorization checks.
Error semantics
401: missing/invalid session.
403: role/AAL2/identity binding insufficient.
404: invitation/application unavailable (avoid token enumeration).
409: used/expired/revoked/state conflict.
422: invalid request or consent missing.
429: rate limit exceeded.
Security requirements
Cache-Control: no-store for identity/application/selfie endpoints.
Never log raw invitation tokens, selfie bytes, access tokens or full Pi token.
Avoid returning email, wallet address, Pi UID or selfie URL to roles that do not need it.
No direct client table writes. RLS remains defense-in-depth; server authorization is mandatory.
No payment, withdrawal or A2U routes are exposed to this role.
